# Project Constitution — ${PROJECT_NAME}

> Stability: **stable**. This document defines the durable values and decision rules that guide specifications, plans, and implementation.

## Product and user commitments

1. `${USER_OUTCOME_COMMITMENT}`
2. `${SAFETY_OR_PRIVACY_COMMITMENT}`
3. `${OPERABILITY_OR_ACCESSIBILITY_COMMITMENT}`

## Engineering commitments

1. Specifications and acceptance evidence precede non-trivial implementation.
2. Each concern has a named source of truth and boundary.
3. Verification depth is proportional to the risk of the change.
4. Architectural decisions are explicit, reversible where possible, and recorded as ADRs.
5. Agents work autonomously only within approved intent and risk boundaries.

## Decision ownership

| Decision class | Accountable owner | Required artifact |
| --- | --- | --- |
| Product scope and acceptance | `${PRODUCT_OWNER}` | Feature spec |
| Architecture and dependencies | `${TECHNICAL_OWNER}` | ADR |
| Security/privacy/compliance | `${RISK_OWNER}` | Threat review or ADR |
| Release acceptance | `${RELEASE_OWNER}` | PR/CI evidence |

## Change rule

Changing this constitution requires an ADR and explicit approval from the accountable owners above.
